us loss of price-insensitive official/bank demand plus levered basis-trade intermediation +75, public-dissaving share +20, UK RPI->CPIH alignment Feb 2030 +7 (the Auditor's dated in-window step: UK breakevens collapse and the measured UK real yield rises 80-100bp at a 0.077 weight — I use his clean +7bp rather than the red-team's practice of burying it in the level), overlap collapsed = +80bp. Expected financial-repression wedge: P = 0.25 at -100bp = -25bp. Swap-versus-breakeven \"or\": P(swaps) = 0.4 at -20bp = -8bp.\nP50 = 1.79 - 0.12 + 0.80 - 0.25 - 0.08 = 2.14 -> 2.1%.\nr-g COHERENCE CHECK WITH MY CQ3 (required by my lens). r rises 1.79 -> 2.14 = +35bp; OECD g falls from a ~1.6-1.8% norm to my 1.15% = -45 to -65bp. Sum = +80 to +100bp, which reproduces 2A's stated ~+1.0pp worsening in (r-g) without my having assumed it. The Reference-Class panelist is right that 2A's (r-g) claim does not pin the LEVEL of r, which is why I derive r from the decomposition and use the identity only as a check.\nCOHERENCE WITH CQ6 TERM-PREMIUM LANGUAGE. CQ6-B (\"steep real term premia\") plus CQ6-C (\"term-premium spikes\") carry 75pp of my mass, which requires a P50 above the 1.79 anchor; +35bp is the modest version of that and is not in tension with D at 9.\nTAILS. P10 = 1.0%. The red-team's constraint is real and I accept it against the Reference-Class panelist's 0.4%: a five-year G7 average near zero now requires the US leg at 48% of the weight to fall ~250bp from +2.60, a larger move than the 1945-70s repression precedents delivered from a comparable start. But the Auditor's perverse case is live in the left tail — if repression arrives as nominal yield caps WITH breakevens blowing out, the nominal-minus-breakeven measure prints negative. P90 = 3.3%: fiscal dominance with the pension/care claim repriced at the long end, Debt-at-Risk realization, dissaving dominant, plus the UK step. Span 2.3pp — tighter than the Reference-Class panelist's 3.0pp because a five-year AVERAGE is sm